card.statement:
Let $(A,B)$ be any pair of matrices of the same size. Write its Kronecker canonical form as follows:

\begin{equation}
(A,B)\ca=
{\cal K}\oplus {\cal P}_1(\lambda_1)
\oplus\dots\oplus {\cal P}_t(\lambda_t),
\quad \lambda_i\ne \lambda _j\text{ if }
i\ne j,\quad \lambda_1,\dots,\lambda_t
\in\mathbb C\cup\infty,
\end{equation}

in which ${\cal K}$ is a direct sum of pairs of the form $(L_k,R_k)$ and $(L_k^T,R_k^T)$, and each ${\cal
P}_i(\lambda_i)$ is a direct sum of pairs of the form ${P}_k(\lambda_i)$. Then the equivalence bundle of $(A,B)$ consists of all matrix pairs whose Kronecker canonical form is

\begin{equation}
{\cal K}\oplus {\cal P}_1(\mu_1)
\oplus\dots\oplus {\cal P}_t(\mu_t),
\quad \mu_i\ne \mu_j\text{ if }
i\ne j,\quad \mu_1,\dots,\mu_t
\in\mathbb C\cup\infty
\end{equation}

with the same ${\cal K},{\cal P}_1,
\dots, {\cal P}_t.$
